BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T113000
SUMMARY:International Speaker Series
DESCRIPTION:Guest lecture followed by Q&amp\;A  Presentation title: "What
 's an Emperor to a Monk? Political Independence in the monastic micro-sta
 te of Mount Athos"  Summary: This talk addresses the Orthodox monastic mi
 cro-state of Mount Athos\, its history\, and government\, through a polit
 ical lens that has rarely been focused on the legendary mountain\, better
  known for its monastery fortresses\, charismatic holy men\, and absolute
  ban on women. Drawing on personal experience\, historical records\, and 
 recent news\, this presentation highlights the inherent conflicts between
  a state that aims to retreat from the world while also maintaining its p
 lace within the Orthodox\, European\, and International order.  Speaker B
 io: Patrick Reilly is a tech consultant\, but more importantly\, a histor
 y\, theology\, and travel-writing enthusiast living in Portland\, Oregon.
  He recently completed a master's degree in Political Science at Portland
  State University\, titled "The Living Dead on Mount Athos: Monastic Poli
 tics of Escape."
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Guest lecture followed by Q&amp\;A</p><
 p>  Presentation title: "What's an Emperor to a Monk? Political Independe
 nce in the monastic micro-state of Mount Athos"</p><p>  Summary: This tal
 k addresses the Orthodox monastic micro-state of Mount Athos\, its histor
 y\, and government\, through a political lens that has rarely been focuse
 d on the legendary mountain\, better known for its monastery fortresses\,
  charismatic holy men\, and absolute ban on women. Drawing on personal ex
 perience\, historical records\, and recent news\, this presentation highl
 ights the inherent conflicts between a state that aims to retreat from th
 e world while also maintaining its place within the Orthodox\, European\,
  and International order.</p><p>  Speaker Bio: Patrick Reilly is a tech c
 onsultant\, but more importantly\, a history\, theology\, and travel-writ
 ing enthusiast living in Portland\, Oregon. He recently completed a maste
 r's degree in Political Science at Portland State University\, titled "Th
 e Living Dead on Mount Athos: Monastic Politics of Escape."</p>
UID:20260423T170000Z-10384@events.pcc.edu
DTSTAMP:20260409T163854Z
URL:https://events.pcc.edu/live/events/10382-international-speaker-series
LAST-MODIFIED:20260409T233854Z
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:10384
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
END:VEVENT
