DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T120000
SUMMARY:Applying for Student Jobs: Stand out on your Application & Resume
DESCRIPTION:Are you a PCC student looking to stand out when applying for 
 on-campus jobs or student leadership roles? This webinar will provide a p
 ractical overview of how to create a compelling application and resume th
 at highlights your strengths\, experiences\, and potential.Designed speci
 fically for those interested in on-campus employment\, this session will 
 review the application and discuss best practices for answering the suppl
 emental questions\, including how to highlight your strengths\, showcase 
 transferable skills\, and tailor your answers for different student posit
 ions. We will also discuss resume basics and why you would include a resu
 me if it's optional.Whether you're applying to be a student advocate\, pe
 er mentor\, student ambassador\, or support staff\, you'll gain tips to h
 elp your application rise to the top.This is an interactive overview sess
 ion—not a working lab—so come ready to learn\, reflect\, and ask ques
 tions. There will be time at the end for Q&amp\;A to address your specifi
 c resume and application concerns.What you'll gain:Key strategies for bui
 lding a strong\, clear application and resumeInsight into what campus emp
 loyers look forTips for highlighting leadership and transferable skillsGu
 idance on tailoring your resume and answers to supplemental questions for
  different opportunitiesBring your questions and leave with the confidenc
 e to take the next step in your campus career!Meeting Link: https://portl
 andcc.zoom.us/meeting/register/TFVsmX_JQQaEet7iAaF1HA#/registration (http
 s://portlandcc.zoom.us/meeting/register/TFVsmX_JQQaEet7iAaF1HA#/registrat
 ion)—Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382667 (https://hub.pcc
 .edu/rsvp?id=382667)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Are you a PCC student looking to stand out w
 hen applying for on-campus jobs or student leadership roles? This webinar
  will provide a practical overview of how to create a compelling applicat
 ion and resume that highlights your strengths\, experiences\, and potenti
 al.<br />Designed specifically for those interested in on-campus employme
 nt\, this session will review the application and discuss best practices 
 for answering the supplemental questions\, including how to highlight you
 r strengths\, showcase transferable skills\, and tailor your answers for 
 different student positions. We will also discuss resume basics and why y
 ou would include a resume if it's optional.<br />Whether you're applying 
 to be a student advocate\, peer mentor\, student ambassador\, or support 
 staff\, you'll gain tips to help your application rise to the top.<br />T
 his is an interactive overview session—not a working lab—so come read
 y to learn\, reflect\, and ask questions. There will be time at the end f
 or Q&amp\;A to address your specific resume and application concerns.<br 
 />What you'll gain:<br />Key strategies for building a strong\, clear app
 lication and resume<br />Insight into what campus employers look for<br /
 >Tips for highlighting leadership and transferable skills<br />Guidance o
