SUMMARY:VOTER REGISTRATION DEADLINE - Oregon Primary Election
DESCRIPTION:The State of Oregon is holding a primary election on Tuesday\
 , May 19th and in order to participate you must be registered to vote on 
 or before April 28th.Reasons to check the status of your voter registrati
 on include:&gt\; If you have moved since the last election&gt\; If you ha
 ve legally changed your name&gt\; If you want to change your political pa
 rtyOregon has closed primary elections\, which means that you can only vo
 te to nominate candidates within the political party they are registered 
 for. This means that you if you want to have say in who the political par
 ty's candidate will be for November's Midterm Election\, then you must be
  register to be a member of that party prior to the primary registration 
 deadline.The election in May will also have the a ballot referendum regar
 ding HB3991\, which would raise the the state gasoline tax from $0.40 per
  gallon to $0.46 per gallon.—Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id
 =382478 (https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382478)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:The State of Oregon is holding a primary ele
 ction on Tuesday\, May 19th and in order to participate you must be regis
 tered to vote on or before April 28th.<br />Reasons to check the status o
 f your voter registration include:<br />&gt\; If you have moved since the
  last election<br />&gt\; If you have legally changed your name<br />&gt\
 ; If you want to change your political party<br />Oregon has closed prima
 ry elections\, which means that you can only vote to nominate candidates 
 within the political party they are registered for. This means that you i
 f you want to have say in who the political party's candidate will be for
  November's Midterm Election\, then you must be register to be a member o
 f that party prior to the primary registration deadline.<br />The electio
 n in May will also have the a ballot referendum regarding HB3991\, which 
 would raise the the state gasoline tax from $0.40 per gallon to $0.46 per
  gallon.<br />—<br />Event Details: <a href="https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?i
 d=382478" target="_blank">https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382478</a>
